        "id": 1499410
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-28T06:52:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It looks like `ublk_open()` is the `ub_fops` open for the block device `/dev/ublkbN`, not for the server\u0027s `/dev/ublkcN`, so this would stop a 4KB process from opening a ublk disk at all, unlike every other block device.\n\nAs far as I can see nothing on that side depends on the opener\u0027s page size: its I/O goes through the block layer as for loop or dm, and only the native server handles ublk\u0027s buffers.\n\nWould it be OK to drop this hunk?",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "e9bdee5e70b33769a30f141e920290997d1aa429",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "08b8d244_d615fd65",
        "filename": "drivers/block/ublk_drv.c",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 1858,
      "author": {
        "id": 1499410
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-28T06:52:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This check looks needed to me, and it is in the right place, before `ub-\u003emm` is claimed: `ublk_ch_mmap()` picks the queue from `vm_pgoff` and checks the length but ignores `vm_slice_off`, while since aosp/4368055 `remap_pfn_range()` starts at slice `vm_slice_off` of the buffer. So an offset that isn\u0027t 16KB-aligned maps memory past the queue\u0027s descriptor buffer, e.g. the first 4KB of the next physical page for a one-page buffer.\n\nCould it use `p3s_4k_unsupported()` (aosp/4366134) instead, as aosp/4368077 and aosp/4368079 do for the ring buffer and vCPU `mmap()`? It logs the refusal with the function name, so refusals hit in production can be identified.\n\nThe new `#include \u003clinux/p3s/mm.h\u003e` shouldn\u0027t be needed either: `\u003clinux/mm_types.h\u003e` already includes it through `\u003clinux/p3s.h\u003e`.",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "e9bdee5e70b33769a30f141e920290997d1aa429",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1f0a3dfb_9fc85b19",
        "filename": "drivers/block/ublk_drv.c",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 2626,
      "author": {
        "id": 1499410
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-28T06:52:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It looks like a 4KB process can\u0027t reach this or `ublk_ctrl_uring_cmd()`: since aosp/4368076, `io_uring_setup()`, `io_uring_enter()` and `io_uring_register()` fail with `-EPERM` in 4KB processes, and SQPOLL and io-wq threads share the mm of the native task that created them, so `current-\u003emm` is always native here.\n\n`/dev/ublk-control` only implements `.uring_cmd`, so the same goes for the new `ublk_ctrl_open()`. This check is also on the per-I/O path.\n\nWould it be OK to drop these three hunks? If you\u0027d like a 4KB server to get a clear error early, the `ublk_ch_open()` check alone would give it.",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "e9bdee5e70b33769a30f141e920290997d1aa429",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a5865db2_bc5891ec",
