        "id": 1499410
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-28T06:52:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think user copy already works in a 4KB process: `ublk_copy_user_pages()` gets the pages with `iov_iter_get_pages2()`, which has taken a 4KB path in `__iov_iter_get_pages_alloc()` since aosp/4312497 (`iov_iter_extract_compat_page()` after aosp/4367612). That returns the kernel page and the slice offset in `off`, and `ublk_copy_io_pages()` copies within those pages. `ublk_map_io()` and `ublk_unmap_io()` use the same function.\n\nWould it be OK to drop this hunk? It is also on the per-I/O path of `UBLK_F_USER_COPY` servers.",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "e9bdee5e70b33769a30f141e920290997d1aa429",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
